{
  "duration": 75.799,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 1.639,
      "text": "So welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.279,
      "end": 3.399,
      "text": "Time for one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 3.859,
      "end": 4.579,
      "text": "Now, in this problem,"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.159,
      "end": 5.879,
      "text": "we are given that"
    },
    {
      "start": 6.399,
      "end": 8.279,
      "text": "the length of the train is"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.96,
      "end": 10.599,
      "text": "one hundred fifty meter."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.159,
      "end": 12.92,
      "text": "The train crosses a pole in ten seconds."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.299,
      "end": 16.719,
      "text": "The question is asking us to find the speed of the train in kilometer per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.219,
      "end": 19.979,
      "text": "And before solving, let us understand one simple concept."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.5,
      "end": 22.079,
      "text": "When a train crosses a pole,"
    },
    {
      "start": 22.579,
      "end": 26.319,
      "text": "it covers only its own length because a pole has no width."
    },
    {
      "start": 26.84,
      "end": 29.479,
      "text": "So the distance covered is simply the length of the train."
    },
    {
      "start": 29.779,
      "end": 30.139,
      "text": "Got it?"
    },
    {
      "start": 30.539,
      "end": 30.92,
      "text": "Perfect."
    },
    {
      "start": 31.319,
      "end": 32.86,
      "text": "Now let us note down the values."
    },
    {
      "start": 33.239,
      "end": 35.799,
      "text": "Distance covered is one hundred fifty meter."
    },
    {
      "start": 36.419,
      "end": 37.759,
      "text": "Time taken is ten seconds."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.18,
      "end": 39.259,
      "text": "We know the basic formula."
    },
    {
      "start": 39.819,
      "end": 42.039,
      "text": "Speed is equal to distance divided by time."
    },
    {
      "start": 42.579,
      "end": 43.459,
      "text": "Putting the values,"
    },
    {
      "start": 43.919,
      "end": 46.5,
      "text": "speed is equal to one hundred fifty divided by ten."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.819,
      "end": 50.019,
      "text": "This gives us fifteen meter per second. Now be very careful here."
    },
    {
      "start": 50.399,
      "end": 53.299,
      "text": "The question is asking for the speed in kilometer per hour,"
    },
    {
      "start": 53.699,
      "end": 57.34,
      "text": "but our answer is in meter per second. So we must convert the units."
    },
    {
      "start": 57.699,
      "end": 62.219,
      "text": "We know that one meter per second is equal to three point six"
    },
    {
      "start": 62.779,
      "end": 64.499,
      "text": "kilometer per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 65.059,
      "end": 72.719,
      "text": "So fifteen into three point six gives us fifty-four kilometer per hour. So the speed of the train is fifty-four kilometer per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 73.199,
      "end": 75.799,
      "text": "Hence the correct answer is option C."
    }
  ],
